---
/**
 * CheckBand — the home page's door into the free check, set as a LEDGER since
 * D113.
 *
 * WHY A BAND AND NOT THE TOOL ITSELF. The check is a React island, and mounting
 * it here would put a second interactive island on a page already measured in
 * thousands of pixels on a phone, and give the page two competing things to do.
 * This is one heading, one paragraph, the arithmetic, and one button.
 *
 * ── WHY IT LOOKS LIKE THIS NOW ──────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * This band and the AI Fit band below it were the same markup with different
 * words — mono label, heading, one muted paragraph, button hard right — sitting
 * back to back, each leaving its middle third empty on a desktop. That pair was
 * a large part of "every section looks like the one before it", which is the
 * complaint D102 ruled on.
 *
 * So this one changes its GROUND, its DENSITY and its RULE WEIGHT, which are
 * three of the five heavy signals `industrial.js` names, and none of them is a
 * color. The result is a band that looks like the arithmetic it is selling: a
 * 3px top rule against hairlines everywhere else, tight rows, tabular figures.
 * The AI Fit band keeps the split-row shape and is now the only band using it.
 *
 * THE LAST ROW CARRIES NO FIGURE, AND THAT IS THE PRODUCT RATHER THAN AN
 * OMISSION. Every number this tool prints is the visitor's own input multiplied
 * out — no model, no benchmark, no industry average. A total sitting in that row
 * would be a figure about nobody, which is the one thing the check exists to
 * refuse. See home.ts's comment on `checkLedger`.
 *
 * IT STAYS ABOVE ANYTHING WITH A PRICE ON IT. Untouched by D113, and the reason
 * this band did not simply move to the foot of the page.
 */
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import { checkLedger } from '../../data/home';
---
<Section tone="deep" density="tight">
  <p class="mono-label">Free · no signup · about a minute</p>
  <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-3xl">
    Start with a number, not a sales pitch.
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[56ch] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
    Two questions about how you order and chase stock, and you will know what the paperwork is
    costing you a year — with the arithmetic printed, so you can check it yourself. Nothing is
    sent anywhere, and there is no email box.
  </p>

  <div class="ledger mt-6">
    <dl>
      {checkLedger.rows.map((r) => (
        <>
          <dt>{r.k}</dt>
          <dd>{r.v}</dd>
        </>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </div>
  <p class="mono-label mt-3">{checkLedger.caption}</p>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <a href="/check/" class="btn btn-primary">Run the free check →</a>
  </div>
</Section>
